    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d488-a1">

                <pb facs="0615" n="507" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg507"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 41.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The prime minister to Mr. McDonald.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-11-19"><hi rendition="#italic">November 19,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: In reply to your letter dated
                    the 27th of Rabbi II, 1311, with reference to the case of Hajie Seyyah,
                    Mahallâti, I beg respectfully to say that Hajie Seyyah, of Mahallât, is a
                    veritable subject of Persia whether he be resident in Persia or he depart for a
                    foreign land. Under no circumstances can there be any change in his nationality,
                    and wherever he may be he will be a citizen of Persia.</p>
                <p>I send this reply so that there may be no objections raised in the future.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <p>[Seal of the prime minister.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
